<Base
  title="About"
  description="A little about Kevin Sherman and the name k10n."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">A little context</p>
    <h1>About this corner.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      I’m Kevin Sherman. This is a personal website, in the ordinary sense of
      both words.
    </p>
    <p>
      I’m interested in software, building things, and understanding how they
      work. There’s room here for the rest of life, too.
    </p>
    <h2>Why k10n?</h2>
    <p>
      It’s a numeronym: the K in Kevin, the N in Sherman, and the ten letters in
      between. A small name for a place that doesn’t need to be about just one
      thing.
    </p>
    <h2>What belongs here</h2>
    <p>
      A useful explanation. A photograph. Something I tried that didn’t work. A
      story that’s still worth telling years later.
    </p>
    <p>
      Not everything needs to become a post, and not every post needs to make a
      point.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
